.TH SH-SIGNAL 1
.SH NAME
signal \- shell script interface to signal(2)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B load signal

.B id := ${signal new}
.br
.B signal
.I id
.B length
.I n
.br
.B signal
.I id
.B tone
.I amplitude frequency
.RI [ phase ]
.br
.B signal
.I id
.B noise
.I amplitude
.RI [ seed ]
.br
.B signal
.I id
.B data
.I value...
.br
.B signal
.I id
.B read
.I file
.br
.B signal
.I id
.B spectrum
.I window
.br
.B signal
.I id
.B fir
.I kind ntaps f1
.RI [ f2 ]
.I window
.br
.B signal
.I id
.B butter
.I kind order fc
.br
.B signal
.I id
.B onepole
.I fc
.br
.B signal
.I id
.B filter
.br
.B signal
.I id
.B response
.I n
.br
.B ${signal
.I id
.BR samples | waveform | taps | trace | names | rows | columns | length | realbins
.B }
.br
.B ${signal
.I id
.B binfreq
.I k
.B }
.br
.B ${signal
.I id
.B peak
.RI [ column ]
.B }
.br
.B signal del
.I id...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Signal
makes
.IR signal (2)
usable from
.IR sh (1).
.PP
.B Frequency
.B is
.B in
.B cycles
.B per
.BR sample ,
0 to 0.5, exactly as in
.IR signal (2):
a sampled signal does not know its own sample rate.
Nyquist is always 0.5.
.SS Building a signal
.B Length
makes a buffer of zeros;
.B tone
and
.B noise
.I add
to whatever is there, so a test signal is built by saying what is in it.
.B Data
and
.B read
replace it instead.
.SS Looking at it
.B Spectrum
computes the one-sided power spectrum under the named window \-
.BR rect ,
.BR hann ,
.B hamming
or
.B blackman
\- scaled so that a sinusoid of amplitude
.I A
reads
.IR A * A /2
in its bin whatever the window.
.PP
.B Peak
returns the row of the last computed series where a column is largest,
the power column by default.
For a spectrum that is the strongest frequency present and how strong,
which is the question a spectrum is usually asked.
.SS Filtering
.B Fir
designs a windowed sinc,
.B butter
a Butterworth cascade and
.B onepole
a single pole; the kinds are
.BR lowpass ,
.BR highpass ,
.B bandpass
and
.BR bandstop .
.B Filter
runs whichever is designed over the samples, in place.
.B Response
records the designed filter's own magnitude and phase from 0 to Nyquist.
.PP
.B Trace
returns whatever series was last computed \- a spectrum or a response \-
as one flat list, which is the shape
.IR sh-plot (1)'s
.B append
takes.
.B Waveform
does the same for the samples, paired with their index.
.SH EXAMPLE
Two tones, a spectrum, and a filter that removes one of them:
.IP
.EX
load std
load signal
s := ${signal new}
signal $s length 256
signal $s tone 2.0 0.0625
signal $s tone 0.5 0.3125
signal $s spectrum hann
echo ${signal $s peak}		# 0.0625 2 - amplitude 2 reads 2
signal $s fir lowpass 63 0.15 hamming
signal $s filter
signal $s spectrum hann
echo ${signal $s peak}		# 0.0625 1.9995 - the other tone is gone
signal del $s
.EE
