.SH DIAGNOSTICS
An even number of taps, a cutoff at or above Nyquist, an order out of
range, a filter run before one is designed: each fails the command, most
with the message
.IR signal (2)
gives.
.SH BUGS
There is no test for this module in
.BR /appl/cmd .
.IR Signal (2)
underneath it is checked by
.IR signaltest (1);
what is added here is the sample buffer, the tone and noise generators
and the flattening, exercised by the example above and by
.BR /lib/demo/spectrumlab.sh .
.PP
.B Filter
replaces the samples, so the original is gone.
Keep a second handle if both are wanted.
.PP
The convolution, correlation and inverse transform of
.IR signal (2)
are not reachable from here, nor is the complex spectrum: only the power
spectrum is, since that is what a plot wants.
.PP
.B Noise
is a linear congruential generator, which is fine for making a signal
look untidy and is not fit for anything that depends on the quality of
its randomness.
